### =====================================================================
### appointMe - requests.http  (Days 5-6)
### Run each request with the green arrow next to it, top to bottom.
### Write down the status code you get and compare with "EXPECTED".
### =====================================================================

### Variables - edit if your ids differ (check: SELECT id, name FROM tenants;)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@tenantId = 1
@otherTenantId = 2
@serviceId = 1


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### TENANTS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### T1. Create tenant            EXPECTED: 201 (note the id in the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Barber",
  "slug": "test-barber",
  "timezone": "Europe/Athens"
}

> {% client.global.set("newTenantId", response.body.id); %}

### T2. Get tenant               EXPECTED: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}

### T3. Get missing tenant       EXPECTED: 500 now, 404 after Day 7
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/9999

### T4. Duplicate slug           EXPECTED: 500 now, 409 after Day 7
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Barber",
  "slug": "test-barber",
  "timezone": "Europe/Athens"
}

### T5. Slug with capitals/space EXPECTED: 400 (pattern check)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Slug",
  "slug": "Test Barber",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### T6. Blank name               EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "slug": "no-name",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### T7. Invalid time zone        EXPECTED: error (400 after Day 7)
###     Works only if you did the ZoneId.of() exercise.
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mars Barber",
  "slug": "mars-barber",
  "timezone": "Mars/Base"
}

### T8. Second tenant (for the isolation test)   EXPECTED: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Second Gym",
  "slug": "second-gym",
  "timezone": "Europe/London"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SERVICES (Day 6)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### S1. Valid create             EXPECTED: 201 (note the service id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": 25.00
}

> {% client.global.set("newServiceId", response.body.id); %}

### S2. Blank name              EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": 25.00
}

### S3. Negative duration       EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": -5,
  "price": 25.00
}

### S4. Missing price          EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30
}

### S5. Negative price         EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": -1
}

### S6. Missing duration       EXPECTED: 400 (this is why the field is Integer, not int)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "price": 25.00
}

### S7. List services          EXPECTED: 200, array
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services

### S8. Get one service       EXPECTED: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### S9. Get missing service    EXPECTED: 500 now, 404 after Day 7
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/9999

### S10. Update (change price) EXPECTED: 200, new price in the body
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "price": 30.00,
  "active": true
}

### S11. Delete (soft)        EXPECTED: 204, row stays with active = false
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### S12. List after delete    EXPECTED: 200 (inactive one still shown unless you did the active-filter exercise)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### ISOLATION CHECK
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### I1. Read tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT the data (500 now, 404 after Day 7)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### I2. Update tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT found, and the service stays unchanged
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hacked",
  "durationMinutes": 1,
  "price": 0.00,
  "active": true
}

### I3. Delete tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT found, and active stays true
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### EXTRA EXPERIMENTS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### X1. Try to sneak in an id   EXPECTED: 201, but the id in the body is ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 99,
  "name": "Sneaky",
  "slug": "sneaky",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### X2. Empty body             EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### X3. Missing Content-Type   EXPECTED: 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants

{"name":"x","slug":"x"}


### C1. Create customer. EXPECT 201, email saved lowercase: "ann@example.com"
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith", "email": "Ann@Example.com", "phone": "6900000001" }

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.id); %}

### C2. Duplicate email, different capitals. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Another Ann", "email": "ANN@example.com" }

### C3. Blank name + bad email. EXPECT 400, errors for fullName and email
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "", "email": "not-an-email" }

### C4a. No email. EXPECT 201 (email is null in the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Walk-in Customer" }

### C4b. Run C4a again. EXPECT 201 again (many customers may have no email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Walk-in Customer" }

### C4c. Blank email string. EXPECT 201, saved as null (not "")
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Blank Email Person", "email": "   " }

### C5. Search + page + sort. EXPECT 200, content has only names containing "ann"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?name=ann&page=0&size=10&sort=fullName,asc

### C5b. Search is case-insensitive. EXPECT same result as C5
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?name=ANN

### C5c. Empty name = no filter. EXPECT every customer, paged
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?name=

### C6. Page 0, size 10. EXPECT 10 items, page 0, totalElements 28+, totalPages 3+
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?page=0&size=10

### C6b. Page 1. EXPECT 10 DIFFERENT items than C6
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?page=1&size=10

### C6c. Page far past the end. EXPECT 200 with "content": []
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?page=999&size=10

### C6d. Descending sort. EXPECT 'Walk-in Customer' / names later in the alphabet first
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?sort=fullName,desc&size=5

### C6e. Size cap. EXPECT "size": 100 in the response, not 100000
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?size=100000

### C7. Bad sort field. EXPECT 400 "Cannot sort by 'nonsense'" (not 500)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?sort=nonsense

### C8. Get one. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### C8b. Missing id. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/999999

### C9. ISOLATION: read tenant 1's customer through tenant 2's URL. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### C9b. ISOLATION: tenant 2 list must not contain tenant 1's customers. EXPECT empty content
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/customers

### C10. Update, keeping the SAME email. EXPECT 200 (must not conflict with itself)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "ann@example.com", "phone": "6900000099" }

### C10b. Update to an email another customer owns. EXPECT 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "c1@test.com" }

### C10c. Update with invalid body. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "" }

### C11. Delete. EXPECT 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### C11b. Delete again. EXPECT 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### C11c. ISOLATION: delete another tenant's customer through your URL. EXPECT 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/customers/1

### N1. EXPECT 200 and a long console log: one "select ... from customers",
###     then one "select ... from tenants where id=?" per distinct tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/debug/n-plus-one